  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "---\n",
    "## 3. Hypothesis Testing\n",
    "\n",
    "**H₀:** Heating milk has no significant effect on ionic calcium activity.\n",
    "\n",
    "**H₁:** Heating milk significantly decreases ionic calcium activity.\n",
    "\n",
    "**α = 0.05**"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "### Test 1: One-Way ANOVA — Does temperature group significantly affect Ca²⁺?"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "control_mM = df[\n",
    "    (df['treatment'] == 'none') &\n",
    "    (df['calcium_activity_mM'].notna()) &\n",
    "    (df['calcium_activity_mM'] < 20)\n",
    "]\n",
    "\n",
    "groups = [g['calcium_activity_mM'].values\n",
    "          for _, g in control_mM.groupby('temperature_C')\n",
    "          if len(g) >= 1]\n",
    "\n",
    "f_stat, p_value = f_oneway(*groups)\n",
    "\n",
    "print('=== One-Way ANOVA ===')\n",
    "print(f'F-statistic : {f_stat:.4f}')\n",
    "print(f'p-value     : {p_value:.6f}')\n",
    "if p_value < 0.05:\n",
    "    print('\\n✅ REJECT H₀: Temperature significantly affects Ca²⁺ activity (p < 0.05).')\n",
    "else:\n",
    "    print('\\n❌ FAIL TO REJECT H₀.')"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "### Test 2: Independent t-test — Unheated vs High Heat (≥90°C)"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "low_temp = control_mM[control_mM['temperature_C'] <= 20]['calcium_activity_mM'].values\n",
    "high_temp = control_mM[control_mM['temperature_C'] >= 90]['calcium_activity_mM'].values\n",
    "\n",
    "t_stat, p_val = ttest_ind(low_temp, high_temp)\n",
    "\n",
    "print('=== Independent t-test: Unheated/Room Temp vs ≥90°C ===')\n",
    "print(f'Low temp mean  : {low_temp.mean():.3f} mM  (n={len(low_temp)})')\n",
    "print(f'High temp mean : {high_temp.mean():.3f} mM  (n={len(high_temp)})')\n",
    "print(f'Reduction      : {((low_temp.mean()-high_temp.mean())/low_temp.mean()*100):.1f}%')\n",
    "print(f't-statistic    : {t_stat:.4f}')\n",
    "print(f'p-value        : {p_val:.6f}')\n",
    "if p_val < 0.05:\n",
    "    print('\\n✅ REJECT H₀: Significant Ca²⁺ reduction at high temperatures (p < 0.05).')\n",
    "else:\n",
    "    print('\\n❌ FAIL TO REJECT H₀.')"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "### Test 3: Pearson Correlation — Temperature vs Ca²⁺"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "corr_data = control_mM[['temperature_C', 'calcium_activity_mM']].dropna()\n",
    "r, p = stats.pearsonr(corr_data['temperature_C'], corr_data['calcium_activity_mM'])\n",
    "\n",
    "print('=== Pearson Correlation ===')\n",
    "print(f'r = {r:.4f},  p = {p:.6f}')\n",
    "if p < 0.05:\n",
    "    strength = 'strong' if abs(r) > 0.7 else 'moderate' if abs(r) > 0.4 else 'weak'\n",
    "    print(f'\\n✅ Significant {\"negative\" if r < 0 else \"positive\"} correlation ({strength}, r={r:.3f}).')\n",
    "else:\n",
    "    print('No significant correlation.')"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "### Test 4: Linear vs Quadratic Fit — Does the decline plateau?"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# Use on_nom2010 — best coverage 20 to 110°C, evenly spaced\n",
    "fit_data = df[(df['source'] == 'on_nom2010') & (df['treatment'] == 'none')].dropna(subset=['calcium_activity_mM'])\n",
    "x = fit_data['temperature_C'].values\n",
    "y = fit_data['calcium_activity_mM'].values\n",
    "\n",
    "lin_coef = np.polyfit(x, y, 1)\n",
    "lin_fit = np.poly1d(lin_coef)\n",
    "lin_r2 = np.corrcoef(y, lin_fit(x))[0,1]**2\n",
    "\n",
    "quad_coef = np.polyfit(x, y, 2)\n",
    "quad_fit = np.poly1d(quad_coef)\n",
    "quad_r2 = np.corrcoef(y, quad_fit(x))[0,1]**2\n",
    "\n",
    "x_plot = np.linspace(x.min(), x.max(), 300)\n",
    "\n",
    "fig, ax = plt.subplots(figsize=(10, 5))\n",
    "ax.scatter(x, y, color='steelblue', s=100, zorder=5, label='On-Nom et al. 2010 data')\n",
    "ax.plot(x_plot, lin_fit(x_plot), 'r--', linewidth=2, label=f'Linear fit  (R²={lin_r2:.3f})')\n",
    "ax.plot(x_plot, quad_fit(x_plot), 'g-', linewidth=2.5, label=f'Quadratic fit (R²={quad_r2:.3f})')\n",
    "\n",
    "ax.set_xlabel('Temperature (°C)', fontsize=12)\n",
    "ax.set_ylabel('Ionic Ca²⁺ Activity (mM)', fontsize=12)\n",
    "ax.set_title('Linear vs Non-linear Fit:\\nDoes Calcium Loss Follow a Diminishing Trend?', fontsize=13)\n",
    "ax.legend(fontsize=10)\n",
    "plt.tight_layout()\n",
    "plt.show()\n",
    "\n",
    "print(f'Linear R²    : {lin_r2:.4f}')\n",
    "print(f'Quadratic R² : {quad_r2:.4f}')\n",
    "if quad_r2 > lin_r2:\n",
    "    print('\\n✅ Quadratic fit is better → supports the diminishing trend hypothesis.')\n",
    "else:\n",
    "    print('\\nLinear fit is sufficient — the decline appears roughly linear in this range.')"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "---\n",
    "## 4. Summary of Findings"
   ]
