   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "print(\"\"\"\n",
    "===========================================================\n",
    "SUMMARY OF RESULTS\n",
    "===========================================================\n",
    "\n",
    "Data: 7 studies spanning 1926–2024, temperatures 0–135°C\n",
    "\n",
    "EDA Findings:\n",
    "- All studies consistently show Ca²⁺ decreasing with temperature\n",
    "- Bovine skim: 1.02–1.22 mM unheated → 0.42–0.65 mM at 80–110°C\n",
    "- pH drops in parallel: confirms Ca-phosphate precipitation mechanism\n",
    "- Sequestering salts (TSC, DSHP) amplify Ca²⁺ loss further\n",
    "- Commercial processing: HTST causes greatest soluble Ca loss\n",
    "- At UHT (121°C): ~7-10% of total calcium lost (retention data)\n",
    "\n",
    "Hypothesis Tests (all at α = 0.05):\n",
    "- ANOVA   : ✅ Temperature group significantly affects Ca²⁺\n",
    "- t-test  : ✅ Unheated vs ≥90°C — significant reduction\n",
    "- Pearson : ✅ Strong negative correlation confirmed\n",
    "- Curve   : ✅ Quadratic > Linear → diminishing trend supported\n",
    "\n",
    "Conclusion:\n",
    "  HYPOTHESIS SUPPORTED — heating milk significantly reduces ionic\n",
    "  calcium activity. The effect is consistent across ~100 years of\n",
    "  research. The trend appears non-linear (diminishing), supporting\n",
    "  the proposed plateau effect at high temperatures.\n",
    "===========================================================\n",
    "\"\"\")"
   ]
  }
